            <h1 style="font-size: 2.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; line-height: 1.2;">
                Looking for a New Goal
            </h1>

            <div style="color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 2rem;">
                Published on July 12, 2026
            </div>

            <div class="blog-content"
                style="color: var(--text-primary); line-height: 1.8; font-size: 1.1rem;">

                <p style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
                    I have not written a blog in a long time, so I thought I would write one today.
                </p>

                <p style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
                    The reason is simple: I am doing fine. I do not really feel lonely anymore. These days, I spend my
                    time playing games for a while, reading Discord chats on my laptop, and listening to music. It may
                    not be the most productive way to spend my days, but that is what my routine has become.
                </p>

                <h2 style="font-size: 1.8rem; margin: 2rem 0 1rem;">
                    Leaving Coding Behind
                </h2>

                <p style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
                    I left coding a long time ago—officially in 2024. Even after that, I would still write some code
                    occasionally in my free time. But now it has been over a month since I last touched it. I think
                    this is where my coding journey truly ends, even as a hobby.
                </p>

                <p style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
                    The problem is that I do not really have a goal anymore. Because of that, I often feel like I am
                    wasting my time. I hope that someday I find something worth grinding for—something that gives me a
                    reason to wake up excited, not just something that earns money.
                </p>

                <h2 style="font-size: 1.8rem; margin: 2rem 0 1rem;">
                    Living with Illness
                </h2>

                <p style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
                    The illness I have been living with has changed the way my brain works. I feel like I process
                    information much more slowly than I used to, and because of that I do not think I can pursue
                    academic goals anymore. It is difficult to accept, but it is how I feel.
                </p>

                <blockquote
                    style="border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-color); padding-left: 1rem; font-style: italic; color: var(--text-secondary); margin: 2rem 0;">
                    Sometimes I think of myself as a failure, but when I look back, I realize that many things happened
                    because of my illness. It changed the path I thought my life would take.
                </blockquote>

                <h2 style="font-size: 1.8rem; margin: 2rem 0 1rem;">
                    Was Computer Science Ever My Passion?
                </h2>

                <p style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
                    I always wanted to become a software engineer, but if I am being honest with myself, I was never
                    very good at programming. Over time, I also realized that I never really enjoyed algorithmic
                    thinking.
                </p>

                <p style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
                    I do not know why I chose Computer Science in the first place. Looking back, I think I chose it
                    simply because I loved using computers. But enjoying computers and enjoying programming are two
                    completely different things.
                </p>

                <p style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
                    To be honest, coding was never my passion. It took me a long time to admit that. And today, AI can
                    write better code than I ever could, which makes me feel even less interested in continuing.
                </p>

                <h2 style="font-size: 1.8rem; margin: 2rem 0 1rem;">
                    Looking Ahead
                </h2>

                <p>
                    I am 24 years old now, and I honestly do not know what comes next. But I hope I find a new
                    goal—something that I genuinely enjoy pursuing, not just for money, but because it gives me
                    happiness and a sense of purpose.
                </p>

                <p style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
                    Maybe this is not the end of my journey. Maybe it is just the end of one chapter and the beginning
                    of another. I just do not know what that next chapter is yet.
                </p>

